d3-react-imperative-chart.promptSeed:
Integrate D3 with React by building an imperative chart bridge that encapsulates direct SVG/D3 DOM manipulation within a child component while exposing a clean control handle to a parent dashboard via `forwardRef` and `useImperativeHandle`.

## Description

Combining D3 and React often presents an architectural conflict: React expects to own and reconcile the DOM tree, while D3 expects direct imperious control over DOM selections, transitions, and calculations.

A proven, production-grade pattern to reconcile them is the **imperative bridge pattern**:
1. The **Child component (`D3BarChart`)** renders a container element (such as an `<svg>`) and anchors D3 via `useRef`. A `useEffect` hook handles D3 scales (`d3.scaleBand()`, `d3.scaleLinear()`), data joins (`selectAll('rect').data(...)`), and element attributes.
2. The child wraps its export in `forwardRef` and uses `useImperativeHandle` to expose a focused control API (`highlight`, `resetHighlight`, `getHighlightedIndex`).
3. The **Parent component (`ChartDashboard`)** holds a ref to the child, renders high-level control buttons ("Highlight Max", "Highlight First", "Reset"), and synchronizes chart interactions with summary status indicators without manipulating raw SVG nodes.

```ts
interface BarDataPoint {
  label: string;
  value: number;
}

interface D3BarChartHandle {
  highlight: (index: number) => void;
  resetHighlight: () => void;
  getHighlightedIndex: () => number | null;
}

interface D3BarChartProps {
  data: BarDataPoint[];
  width?: number;
  height?: number;
  onSelectBar?: (item: BarDataPoint | null, index: number | null) => void;
}

interface ChartDashboardProps {
  data: BarDataPoint[];
  width?: number;
  height?: number;
}
```

### `D3BarChart(props: D3BarChartProps, ref: any)`
A `forwardRef` component that renders an SVG bar chart using D3:
- Renders an `<svg>` with attributes `width={width}`, `height={height}`, `role="img"`, and `aria-label="Bar chart"`. Default `width` is `300`, default `height` is `150`.
- Computes layout with D3:
  - An x-scale with `d3.scaleBand()` spanning the item indices `[0, 1, ..., data.length - 1]` mapped to range `[margin.left, width - margin.right]`.
  - A y-scale with `d3.scaleLinear()` mapping values `[0, d3.max(data, d => d.value) || 1]` to range `[height - margin.bottom, margin.top]`. (Using default margins: top: 10, right: 10, bottom: 20, left: 10).
- Renders a `<rect>` for each data point:
  - `data-index={index}`
  - `data-label={d.label}`
  - `data-value={d.value}`
  - `data-highlighted={index === highlightedIndex ? "true" : "false"}`
  - `x`, `y`, `width`, and `height` derived from the D3 scales.
  - Clicking any bar selects/highlights that bar and calls `onSelectBar?.(item, index)`.
- Exposes via `useImperativeHandle`:
  - `highlight(index: number)`: highlights the bar at `index` (sets `data-highlighted="true"` on that bar and `"false"` on others) and calls `onSelectBar?.(data[index] ?? null, index)`.
  - `resetHighlight()`: removes highlight from all bars and calls `onSelectBar?.(null, null)`.
  - `getHighlightedIndex()`: returns the currently highlighted index (`number` or `null`).

### `ChartDashboard({ data, width = 300, height = 150 }: ChartDashboardProps)`
A parent dashboard component that controls and displays `D3BarChart`:
- Maintains a ref `const chartRef = useRef<D3BarChartHandle | null>(null);`.
- Maintains state for the currently selected item (updated via `onSelectBar`).
- Renders:
  - Container `<div className="chart-dashboard">`.
  - Control bar `<div className="chart-controls">`:
    - `<button data-action="highlight-max">Highlight Max</button>`: finds the index of the item with the highest `value` in `data` and calls `chartRef.current?.highlight(maxIndex)`.
    - `<button data-action="highlight-first">Highlight First</button>`: calls `chartRef.current?.highlight(0)` if data is not empty.
    - `<button data-action="reset">Reset</button>`: calls `chartRef.current?.resetHighlight()`.
  - Status readout element `<div data-testid="status">`:
    - Displays `"No selection"` when nothing is highlighted.
    - Displays `Selected: ${selected.label} (${selected.value})` when a bar is selected.
  - The chart component: `<D3BarChart ref={chartRef} data={data} width={width} height={height} onSelectBar={...} />`.

d3-react-imperative-chart.testHarness:
const { render, fire, q, qa, act } = $dom;

const SAMPLE_DATA = [
  { label: 'A', value: 10 },
  { label: 'B', value: 40 },
  { label: 'C', value: 25 },
];

// 1. Initial render mounts SVG and uses D3 to create data-joined rect elements
{
  const r = render(<ChartDashboard data={SAMPLE_DATA} />);
  const svg = q('svg', r.container);
  const bars = qa('rect', r.container);
  const statusEl = q('[data-testid="status"]', r.container);

  const passed =
    svg !== null &&
    svg.getAttribute('role') === 'img' &&
    bars.length === 3 &&
    bars[0].getAttribute('data-label') === 'A' &&
    bars[0].getAttribute('data-value') === '10' &&
    bars[1].getAttribute('data-label') === 'B' &&
    bars[1].getAttribute('data-value') === '40' &&
    statusEl !== null &&
    statusEl.textContent.trim() === 'No selection';

  $test.check(
    'Initial render mounts SVG and uses D3 to create data-joined rect elements',
    passed,
    { hasSvg: !!svg, barCount: bars.length, status: statusEl?.textContent }
  );
  r.unmount();
}

// 2. Clicking Highlight Max triggers parent control to call imperative handle on maximum bar
{
  const r = render(<ChartDashboard data={SAMPLE_DATA} />);
  const maxBtn = q('button[data-action="highlight-max"]', r.container);
  if (maxBtn) fire.click(maxBtn);

  const bars = qa('rect', r.container);
  const statusEl = q('[data-testid="status"]', r.container);

  const bar0Highlighted = bars[0]?.getAttribute('data-highlighted') === 'true';
  const bar1Highlighted = bars[1]?.getAttribute('data-highlighted') === 'true';
  const bar2Highlighted = bars[2]?.getAttribute('data-highlighted') === 'true';
  const statusMatches = statusEl?.textContent.includes('Selected: B (40)');

  $test.check(
    'Clicking Highlight Max triggers parent control to call imperative handle on maximum bar',
    !bar0Highlighted && bar1Highlighted && !bar2Highlighted && !!statusMatches,
    { bar0Highlighted, bar1Highlighted, bar2Highlighted, status: statusEl?.textContent }
  );
  r.unmount();
}

// 3. Clicking Reset clears the highlighted bar and restores status
{
  const r = render(<ChartDashboard data={SAMPLE_DATA} />);
  const maxBtn = q('button[data-action="highlight-max"]', r.container);
  const resetBtn = q('button[data-action="reset"]', r.container);

  if (maxBtn) fire.click(maxBtn);
  if (resetBtn) fire.click(resetBtn);

  const bars = qa('rect', r.container);
  const statusEl = q('[data-testid="status"]', r.container);

  const anyHighlighted = bars.some((b) => b.getAttribute('data-highlighted') === 'true');
  const statusCleared = statusEl?.textContent.trim() === 'No selection';

  $test.check(
    'Clicking Reset clears the highlighted bar and restores status',
    !anyHighlighted && statusCleared,
    { anyHighlighted, status: statusEl?.textContent }
  );
  r.unmount();
}

// 4. Clicking Highlight First targets index 0
{
  const r = render(<ChartDashboard data={SAMPLE_DATA} />);
  const firstBtn = q('button[data-action="highlight-first"]', r.container);
  if (firstBtn) fire.click(firstBtn);

  const bars = qa('rect', r.container);
  const statusEl = q('[data-testid="status"]', r.container);

  const bar0Highlighted = bars[0]?.getAttribute('data-highlighted') === 'true';
  const bar1Highlighted = bars[1]?.getAttribute('data-highlighted') === 'true';
  const statusMatches = statusEl?.textContent.includes('Selected: A (10)');

  $test.check(
    'Clicking Highlight First targets index 0',
    bar0Highlighted && !bar1Highlighted && !!statusMatches,
    { bar0Highlighted, status: statusEl?.textContent }
  );
  r.unmount();
}

// 5. Direct imperative calls through ref (highlight, resetHighlight, getHighlightedIndex)
{
  let exposedHandle = null;
  function TestWrapper() {
    const ref = useRef(null);
    useEffect(() => {
      exposedHandle = ref.current;
    });
    return <D3BarChart ref={ref} data={[{ label: 'X', value: 5 }, { label: 'Y', value: 15 }]} />;
  }

  const r = render(<TestWrapper />);
  let initialIdx = null;
  let midIdx = null;
  let endIdx = null;

  if (exposedHandle) {
    initialIdx = exposedHandle.getHighlightedIndex();
    act(() => {
      exposedHandle.highlight(1);
    });
    midIdx = exposedHandle.getHighlightedIndex();
    act(() => {
      exposedHandle.resetHighlight();
    });
    endIdx = exposedHandle.getHighlightedIndex();
  }

  const passed =
    exposedHandle !== null &&
    typeof exposedHandle.highlight === 'function' &&
    typeof exposedHandle.resetHighlight === 'function' &&
    typeof exposedHandle.getHighlightedIndex === 'function' &&
    initialIdx === null &&
    midIdx === 1 &&
    endIdx === null;

  $test.check(
    'Direct imperative calls through ref update D3BarChart state and return active index',
    passed,
    { initialIdx, midIdx, endIdx }
  );
  r.unmount();
}

// 6. Direct click on SVG bar triggers onSelectBar and highlights the clicked bar
{
  const r = render(<ChartDashboard data={SAMPLE_DATA} />);
  const bars = qa('rect', r.container);
  if (bars[2]) fire.click(bars[2]);

  const bar2Highlighted = bars[2]?.getAttribute('data-highlighted') === 'true';
  const statusEl = q('[data-testid="status"]', r.container);
  const statusMatches = statusEl?.textContent.includes('Selected: C (25)');

  $test.check(
    'Direct click on SVG bar triggers onSelectBar and highlights the clicked bar',
    bar2Highlighted && !!statusMatches,
    { bar2Highlighted, status: statusEl?.textContent }
  );
  r.unmount();
}

d3-react-imperative-chart.referenceSolution:
const D3BarChart = forwardRef(function D3BarChart(
  { data, width = 300, height = 150, onSelectBar },
  ref
) {
  const svgRef = useRef(null);
  const [highlightedIndex, setHighlightedIndex] = useState(null);
  const highlightedRef = useRef(null);
  highlightedRef.current = highlightedIndex;

  const selectBar = useCallback(
    (index) => {
      if (index === null || index < 0 || !data || index >= data.length) {
        setHighlightedIndex(null);
        if (typeof onSelectBar === 'function') onSelectBar(null, null);
      } else {
        setHighlightedIndex(index);
        if (typeof onSelectBar === 'function') onSelectBar(data[index], index);
      }
    },
    [data, onSelectBar]
  );

  useImperativeHandle(
    ref,
    () => ({
      highlight(index) {
        selectBar(index);
      },
      resetHighlight() {
        selectBar(null);
      },
      getHighlightedIndex() {
        return highlightedRef.current;
      },
    }),
    [selectBar]
  );

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!svgRef.current || !data || data.length === 0) return;

    const svg = d3.select(svgRef.current);
    const margin = { top: 10, right: 10, bottom: 20, left: 10 };
    const chartWidth = Math.max(0, width - margin.left - margin.right);
    const chartHeight = Math.max(0, height - margin.top - margin.bottom);

    const x = d3
      .scaleBand()
      .domain(data.map((_, i) => String(i)))
      .range([margin.left, margin.left + chartWidth])
      .padding(0.2);

    const maxVal = d3.max(data, (d) => d.value) || 1;
    const y = d3
      .scaleLinear()
      .domain([0, maxVal])
      .range([margin.top + chartHeight, margin.top]);

    const bars = svg.selectAll('rect').data(data, (_, i) => String(i));

    bars.exit().remove();

    bars
      .enter()
      .append('rect')
      .merge(bars)
      .attr('data-index', (_, i) => i)
      .attr('data-label', (d) => d.label)
      .attr('data-value', (d) => d.value)
      .attr('x', (_, i) => x(String(i)) || 0)
      .attr('y', (d) => y(d.value))
      .attr('width', x.bandwidth())
      .attr('height', (d) => Math.max(0, margin.top + chartHeight - y(d.value)))
      .attr('data-highlighted', (_, i) => (i === highlightedIndex ? 'true' : 'false'))
      .attr('fill', (_, i) => (i === highlightedIndex ? 'orange' : 'steelblue'))
      .on('click', (_, d) => {
        const idx = data.indexOf(d);
        selectBar(idx);
      });
  }, [data, width, height, highlightedIndex, selectBar]);

  return (
    <svg
      ref={svgRef}
      width={width}
      height={height}
      role="img"
      aria-label="Bar chart"
    />
  );
});

function ChartDashboard({ data, width = 300, height = 150 }) {
  const chartRef = useRef(null);
  const [selected, setSelected] = useState(null);

  const handleHighlightMax = () => {
    if (!data || data.length === 0) return;
    let maxIdx = 0;
    for (let i = 1; i < data.length; i++) {
      if (data[i].value > data[maxIdx].value) {
        maxIdx = i;
      }
    }
    chartRef.current?.highlight(maxIdx);
  };

  const handleHighlightFirst = () => {
    if (data && data.length > 0) {
      chartRef.current?.highlight(0);
    }
  };

  const handleReset = () => {
    chartRef.current?.resetHighlight();
  };

  return (
    <div className="chart-dashboard">
      <div className="chart-controls">
        <button
          type="button"
          data-action="highlight-max"
          onClick={handleHighlightMax}
        >
          Highlight Max
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-action="highlight-first"
          onClick={handleHighlightFirst}
        >
          Highlight First
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-action="reset"
          onClick={handleReset}
        >
          Reset
        </button>
      </div>

      <div data-testid="status">
        {selected ? `Selected: ${selected.label} (${selected.value})` : 'No selection'}
      </div>

      <D3BarChart
        ref={chartRef}
        data={data}
        width={width}
        height={height}
        onSelectBar={(item) => setSelected(item)}
      />
    </div>
  );
}

