d3-brush-zoom-coordinator.promptSeed:
### `renderBrushCoordinator(container: HTMLElement, data: BrushPoint[], options?: BrushCoordinatorOptions): BrushCoordinatorInstance`

## Description

```ts
interface BrushPoint {
  x: number;
  y: number;
}

interface BrushCoordinatorOptions {
  width?: number;
  focusHeight?: number;
  contextHeight?: number;
  color?: string;
  initialSelection?: [number, number];
  onBrushChange?: (domain: [number, number], filteredData: BrushPoint[]) => void;
}

interface BrushCoordinatorInstance {
  svg: SVGSVGElement;
  getDomain: () => [number, number];
  getFilteredData: () => BrushPoint[];
  setBrushDomain: (domain: [number, number] | null) => void;
  destroy: () => void;
}
```

Linked **focus + context** charts pair a detailed primary chart ("focus") with a compact overview mini-map ("context") below it. Dragging or resizing a 1D horizontal brush (`d3.brushX()`) across the context mini-map rescales the focus chart's X domain in real time via `scale.invert()`.

Implement `renderBrushCoordinator(container, data, options)` to mount a synchronized focus + context SVG visualization with interactive brushing and programmatic domain control.

### Requirements

- **Canvas & Layout Geometry**:
  - Empties `container.innerHTML` before mounting.
  - Option defaults: `width = 480`, `focusHeight = 200`, `contextHeight = 70`, `color = 'steelblue'`.
  - Uses margin `{ top: 15, right: 20, bottom: 25, left: 40 }` and vertical `gap = 25` between the focus and context charts.
  - Computes `innerWidth = Math.max(0, width - margin.left - margin.right)` and `totalHeight = focusHeight + contextHeight + gap + margin.top + margin.bottom`.
  - Appends `<svg>` with `width={width}` and `height={totalHeight}`.

- **Scales & Groups**:
  - Derives `fullDomain: [number, number]` from `d3.extent(data, d => d.x)` (fallback `[0, 1]` when empty) and `yDomain: [number, number]` from `[0, d3.max(data, d => d.y) || 1]`.
  - Configures `focusX` and `contextX` (`d3.scaleLinear().domain(fullDomain).range([0, innerWidth])`), `focusY` (`range([focusHeight, 0])`), and `contextY` (`range([contextHeight, 0])`).
  - Appends `<g class="focus-chart">` translated to `translate(margin.left, margin.top)` containing:
    - `<path class="focus-line">` (`fill="none"`, `stroke={color}`, `stroke-width="2"`)
    - `<g class="focus-dots">` containing `<circle class="focus-dot">` elements for points inside the active domain (`d.x >= domain[0] && d.x <= domain[1]`), with `cx`, `cy`, `r="3.5"`, `fill={color}`, `data-x={String(d.x)}`, and `data-y={String(d.y)}`
    - `<g class="x-axis focus-x-axis">` at `translate(0, focusHeight)` calling `d3.axisBottom(focusX)`
    - `<g class="y-axis focus-y-axis">` calling `d3.axisLeft(focusY)`
  - Appends `<g class="context-chart">` translated to `translate(margin.left, margin.top + focusHeight + gap)` containing:
    - `<path class="context-line">` (`fill="none"`, `stroke="gray"`, `stroke-width="1.5"`) rendering all data points
    - `<g class="x-axis context-x-axis">` at `translate(0, contextHeight)` calling `d3.axisBottom(contextX)`
    - `<g class="brush-layer">` calling `d3.brushX().extent([[0, 0], [innerWidth, contextHeight]])`

- **Brush Coordination & Instance API**:
  - When the brush fires (`'brush end'`), if `event.selection` is `[px0, px1]`, converts pixel bounds to data domain `[contextX.invert(px0), contextX.invert(px1)]`; if `event.selection` is `null`, resets to `fullDomain`.
  - Updating the active domain updates `focusX.domain(currentDomain)`, re-renders `path.focus-line`, `circle.focus-dot` (only points within `currentDomain`), and `g.focus-x-axis`, and invokes `options.onBrushChange(currentDomain, filteredData)` if provided.
  - If `options.initialSelection` is provided, applies that domain on initialization.
  - `getDomain()`: returns `[currentDomain[0], currentDomain[1]]`.
  - `getFilteredData()`: returns points with `d.x >= currentDomain[0] && d.x <= currentDomain[1]`.
  - `setBrushDomain(domain)`: programmatically sets the active domain `[minX, maxX]` (moving the brush selection to `[contextX(minX), contextX(maxX)]`) or resets to `fullDomain` when `null` is passed, updating the focus view and firing `onBrushChange`.
  - `destroy()`: removes the SVG element and clears `container.innerHTML`.

d3-brush-zoom-coordinator.testHarness:
const SAMPLE_SERIES = [
  { x: 0, y: 20 },
  { x: 10, y: 45 },
  { x: 20, y: 30 },
  { x: 30, y: 80 },
  { x: 40, y: 65 },
  { x: 50, y: 90 },
];

// 1. Mounts SVG with focus and context chart groups and brush layer
{
  const container = document.createElement('div');
  document.body.appendChild(container);

  const instance = renderBrushCoordinator(container, SAMPLE_SERIES, {
    width: 500,
    focusHeight: 180,
    contextHeight: 60,
  });

  const svg = container.querySelector('svg');
  const focusChart = container.querySelector('g.focus-chart');
  const contextChart = container.querySelector('g.context-chart');
  const brushLayer = container.querySelector('g.brush-layer');
  const focusDots = container.querySelectorAll('circle.focus-dot');

  const expectedHeight = String(180 + 60 + 25 + 15 + 25);

  const passed =
    svg !== null &&
    svg.getAttribute('width') === '500' &&
    svg.getAttribute('height') === expectedHeight &&
    focusChart !== null &&
    contextChart !== null &&
    brushLayer !== null &&
    focusDots.length === 6 &&
    instance.svg === svg;

  $test.check(
    'Mounts SVG with focus and context chart groups and brush layer',
    passed,
    {
      width: svg?.getAttribute('width'),
      height: svg?.getAttribute('height'),
      dots: focusDots.length,
    }
  );

  instance.destroy();
  container.remove();
}

// 2. Renders focus and context line paths with full initial domain
{
  const container = document.createElement('div');
  document.body.appendChild(container);

  const instance = renderBrushCoordinator(container, SAMPLE_SERIES, {
    color: 'teal',
  });

  const focusLine = container.querySelector('path.focus-line');
  const contextLine = container.querySelector('path.context-line');
  const domain = instance.getDomain();
  const filtered = instance.getFilteredData();

  const passed =
    focusLine !== null &&
    (focusLine.getAttribute('d') || '').startsWith('M') &&
    focusLine.getAttribute('stroke') === 'teal' &&
    contextLine !== null &&
    (contextLine.getAttribute('d') || '').startsWith('M') &&
    domain[0] === 0 &&
    domain[1] === 50 &&
    filtered.length === 6;

  $test.check(
    'Renders focus and context line paths with full initial domain',
    passed,
    { domain, filteredCount: filtered.length, stroke: focusLine?.getAttribute('stroke') }
  );

  instance.destroy();
  container.remove();
}

// 3. Applies initialSelection on mount and filters focus dots to active window
{
  const container = document.createElement('div');
  document.body.appendChild(container);

  const instance = renderBrushCoordinator(container, SAMPLE_SERIES, {
    initialSelection: [10, 30],
  });

  const domain = instance.getDomain();
  const filtered = instance.getFilteredData();
  const dots = Array.from(container.querySelectorAll('circle.focus-dot'));
  const dotXs = dots.map((c) => Number(c.getAttribute('data-x')));

  const passed =
    Math.abs(domain[0] - 10) < 1e-6 &&
    Math.abs(domain[1] - 30) < 1e-6 &&
    filtered.length === 3 &&
    dots.length === 3 &&
    dotXs[0] === 10 &&
    dotXs[1] === 20 &&
    dotXs[2] === 30;

  $test.check(
    'Applies initialSelection on mount and filters focus dots to active window',
    passed,
    { domain, dotXs }
  );

  instance.destroy();
  container.remove();
}

// 4. Updating domain via setBrushDomain rescales focus view and fires onBrushChange
{
  const container = document.createElement('div');
  document.body.appendChild(container);

  let lastDomain = null;
  let lastFiltered = null;

  const instance = renderBrushCoordinator(container, SAMPLE_SERIES, {
    onBrushChange: (dom, pts) => {
      lastDomain = dom;
      lastFiltered = pts;
    },
  });

  instance.setBrushDomain([20, 40]);

  const domainAfterSet = instance.getDomain();
  const dotsAfterSet = container.querySelectorAll('circle.focus-dot');
  // At domain [20, 40], x=20 maps to cx=0 and x=40 maps to cx=innerWidth (420)
  const firstDotCx = Number(dotsAfterSet[0]?.getAttribute('cx'));
  const lastDotCx = Number(dotsAfterSet[dotsAfterSet.length - 1]?.getAttribute('cx'));

  const passed =
    lastDomain !== null &&
    Math.abs(lastDomain[0] - 20) < 1e-6 &&
    Math.abs(lastDomain[1] - 40) < 1e-6 &&
    Array.isArray(lastFiltered) &&
    lastFiltered.length === 3 &&
    Math.abs(domainAfterSet[0] - 20) < 1e-6 &&
    Math.abs(domainAfterSet[1] - 40) < 1e-6 &&
    dotsAfterSet.length === 3 &&
    Math.abs(firstDotCx - 0) < 1e-4 &&
    Math.abs(lastDotCx - 420) < 1e-4;

  $test.check(
    'Updating domain via setBrushDomain rescales focus view and fires onBrushChange',
    passed,
    { lastDomain, dotsCount: dotsAfterSet.length, firstDotCx, lastDotCx }
  );

  instance.destroy();
  container.remove();
}

// 5. Clearing brush selection with null restores full domain and all data points
{
  const container = document.createElement('div');
  document.body.appendChild(container);

  const instance = renderBrushCoordinator(container, SAMPLE_SERIES, {
    initialSelection: [10, 20],
  });

  const narrowedCount = instance.getFilteredData().length;
  instance.setBrushDomain(null);
  const restoredDomain = instance.getDomain();
  const restoredCount = instance.getFilteredData().length;
  const restoredDots = container.querySelectorAll('circle.focus-dot').length;

  const passed =
    narrowedCount === 2 &&
    restoredDomain[0] === 0 &&
    restoredDomain[1] === 50 &&
    restoredCount === 6 &&
    restoredDots === 6;

  $test.check(
    'Clearing brush selection with null restores full domain and all data points',
    passed,
    { narrowedCount, restoredDomain, restoredCount, restoredDots }
  );

  instance.destroy();
  container.remove();
}

// 6. Handles empty data gracefully and cleans up DOM on destroy
{
  const container = document.createElement('div');
  document.body.appendChild(container);

  const emptyInstance = renderBrushCoordinator(container, []);
  const emptyDomain = emptyInstance.getDomain();
  const emptyFiltered = emptyInstance.getFilteredData();
  emptyInstance.destroy();
  const cleanedUp = container.innerHTML === '';

  const passed =
    Array.isArray(emptyDomain) &&
    emptyDomain.length === 2 &&
    Array.isArray(emptyFiltered) &&
    emptyFiltered.length === 0 &&
    cleanedUp;

  $test.check(
    'Handles empty data gracefully and cleans up DOM on destroy',
    passed,
    { emptyDomain, emptyFilteredCount: emptyFiltered.length, cleanedUp }
  );

  container.remove();
}

d3-brush-zoom-coordinator.referenceSolution:
function renderBrushCoordinator(container, data = [], options = {}) {
  const {
    width = 480,
    focusHeight = 200,
    contextHeight = 70,
    color = 'steelblue',
    initialSelection,
    onBrushChange,
  } = options;

  const margin = { top: 15, right: 20, bottom: 25, left: 40 };
  const gap = 25;
  const innerWidth = Math.max(0, width - margin.left - margin.right);
  const totalHeight = focusHeight + contextHeight + gap + margin.top + margin.bottom;

  container.innerHTML = '';

  const points = Array.isArray(data) ? data : [];
  const xExt = d3.extent(points, (d) => d.x);
  const fullDomain =
    xExt[0] !== undefined && xExt[1] !== undefined ? [xExt[0], xExt[1]] : [0, 1];
  const maxY = d3.max(points, (d) => d.y);
  const yDomain = [0, maxY !== undefined && maxY > 0 ? maxY : 1];

  let currentDomain = [fullDomain[0], fullDomain[1]];

  const focusX = d3.scaleLinear().domain(currentDomain).range([0, innerWidth]);
  const focusY = d3.scaleLinear().domain(yDomain).range([focusHeight, 0]);
  const contextX = d3.scaleLinear().domain(fullDomain).range([0, innerWidth]);
  const contextY = d3.scaleLinear().domain(yDomain).range([contextHeight, 0]);

  const svg = d3
    .select(container)
    .append('svg')
    .attr('width', width)
    .attr('height', totalHeight);

  const focusGroup = svg
    .append('g')
    .attr('class', 'focus-chart')
    .attr('transform', `translate(${margin.left}, ${margin.top})`);

  const contextGroup = svg
    .append('g')
    .attr('class', 'context-chart')
    .attr('transform', `translate(${margin.left}, ${margin.top + focusHeight + gap})`);

  const focusLineGen = d3
    .line()
    .x((d) => focusX(d.x))
    .y((d) => focusY(d.y));

  const contextLineGen = d3
    .line()
    .x((d) => contextX(d.x))
    .y((d) => contextY(d.y));

  const focusPath = focusGroup
    .append('path')
    .attr('class', 'focus-line')
    .attr('fill', 'none')
    .attr('stroke', color)
    .attr('stroke-width', 2);

  const focusDotsGroup = focusGroup.append('g').attr('class', 'focus-dots');

  const focusXAxisGroup = focusGroup
    .append('g')
    .attr('class', 'x-axis focus-x-axis')
    .attr('transform', `translate(0, ${focusHeight})`);

  focusGroup
    .append('g')
    .attr('class', 'y-axis focus-y-axis')
    .call(d3.axisLeft(focusY));

  contextGroup
    .append('path')
    .attr('class', 'context-line')
    .attr('fill', 'none')
    .attr('stroke', 'gray')
    .attr('stroke-width', 1.5)
    .attr('d', points.length > 0 ? contextLineGen(points) : '');

  contextGroup
    .append('g')
    .attr('class', 'x-axis context-x-axis')
    .attr('transform', `translate(0, ${contextHeight})`)
    .call(d3.axisBottom(contextX));

  function getFilteredData() {
    return points.filter((d) => d.x >= currentDomain[0] && d.x <= currentDomain[1]);
  }

  function updateFocusView(nextDomain, notify = false) {
    const d0 = Math.min(nextDomain[0], nextDomain[1]);
    const d1 = Math.max(nextDomain[0], nextDomain[1]);
    currentDomain = [d0, d1];
    focusX.domain(currentDomain);

    const visible = getFilteredData();
    focusPath.attr('d', visible.length > 0 ? focusLineGen(visible) : '');

    focusDotsGroup
      .selectAll('circle.focus-dot')
      .data(visible)
      .join('circle')
      .attr('class', 'focus-dot')
      .attr('cx', (d) => focusX(d.x))
      .attr('cy', (d) => focusY(d.y))
      .attr('r', 3.5)
      .attr('fill', color)
      .attr('data-x', (d) => String(d.x))
      .attr('data-y', (d) => String(d.y));

    focusXAxisGroup.call(d3.axisBottom(focusX));

    if (notify && typeof onBrushChange === 'function') {
      onBrushChange([currentDomain[0], currentDomain[1]], visible);
    }
  }

  const brush = d3
    .brushX()
    .extent([
      [0, 0],
      [innerWidth, contextHeight],
    ])
    .on('brush end', function (event) {
      if (event && Array.isArray(event.selection)) {
        const [px0, px1] = event.selection;
        updateFocusView([contextX.invert(px0), contextX.invert(px1)], true);
      } else {
        updateFocusView(fullDomain, true);
      }
    });

  const brushGroup = contextGroup
    .append('g')
    .attr('class', 'brush-layer')
    .call(brush);

  updateFocusView(fullDomain, false);

  function setBrushDomain(domain) {
    if (!domain || !Array.isArray(domain)) {
      try {
        brushGroup.call(brush.move, null);
      } catch (_) {}
      updateFocusView(fullDomain, true);
    } else {
      const d0 = Math.min(domain[0], domain[1]);
      const d1 = Math.max(domain[0], domain[1]);
      try {
        brushGroup.call(brush.move, [contextX(d0), contextX(d1)]);
      } catch (_) {}
      updateFocusView([d0, d1], true);
    }
  }

  if (Array.isArray(initialSelection) && initialSelection.length === 2) {
    setBrushDomain(initialSelection);
  }

  return {
    svg: svg.node(),
    getDomain() {
      return [currentDomain[0], currentDomain[1]];
    },
    getFilteredData,
    setBrushDomain,
    destroy() {
      svg.remove();
      container.innerHTML = '';
    },
  };
}

